Previous failing build (reported by the parent, retained for traceability):

  /prod/sonrisa_homework/src/api/Selection/AlertSelectionService.cs(157,22): error CS1503:
  Argument 1: cannot convert from 'System.TimeSpan' to 'decimal'

  Cause: Math.Abs has no TimeSpan overload (TimeSpan.Abs() is the instance method).
  Fix: the alignment check now compares TimeSpans directly and keeps the stated
  one-minute tolerance; DateTimeOffset safety guards were added in the same method:
    - observation time below DateTimeOffset.MinValue + 24h -> no baseline (no underflow)
    - a baseline later than the observation is rejected (not a 24-hour-earlier value)
    - |BaselineUtc - (ObservationUtc - 24h)| <= 1 minute, measured with TimeSpan.Duration()

